            </h3>
            <p class="text-xs text-slate-300 leading-relaxed">
              With a strict 512-token ceiling, BGE-Reranker-Large requires aggressive chunking during indexing. If your knowledge base contains complex API schemas, judicial opinions, or medical trial protocols, chunks that span 700+ tokens will have their trailing text silently chopped off prior to the cross-attention layer.
            </p>
            <ul class="text-xs space-y-2 list-disc list-inside text-slate-400">
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Recommended Chunk Size:</strong> Max 350 tokens + 50 token overlap to reserve 112 tokens for multi-turn user queries.</li>
              <li><strong class="text-slate-200">Late Chunking Mitigation:</strong> Pass whole documents through long-context bi-encoders first, then slice embedding pooled states to preserve holistic meaning.</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/60 border border-cyan-500/30 space-y-3">
            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-white flex items-center gap-2">
